---
/**
 * Homepage — Approved Contractor, Inc. (ambush concept build).
 *
 * THE ONE-SENTENCE IDEA
 * ---------------------
 * Approved Contractor only builds the one part of a house its owner never
 * looks at and every neighbour does — so the page is that part, drawn as an
 * architectural ELEVATION, annotated, and stamped with their own name.
 *
 * The idea is structural, not decorative. It decides:
 *   HERO      a drawn front elevation with the six trades called out on
 *             leaders, dimensioned across the bottom with the sentence the
 *             whole page is built on.
 *   SERVICES  not a card grid — the drawing's LEGEND. Bubble 03 on the facade
 *             is line 03 in the key, and both derive the number from position
 *             in the same collection, so they cannot drift apart.
 *   RECORD    the plan sheet's title block: the mark, the licence, the
 *             counties, the figures. Ruled like a document because reading
 *             like a document is the argument.
 *   TYPE      an expanded grotesque, because every architectural drawing set
 *             on earth is labelled in one, plus a mono that carries every
 *             number on the page.
 *
 * WHAT IS NOT HERE, AND WHY (CLAUDE.md §11)
 * ------------------------------------------
 * Three sections are wired, imported and ready, and render the moment content
 * exists. They ship as nothing rather than as something invented:
 *
 *   BeforeAfter     `projects` is empty. Zero job photographs were supplied.
 *                   For an exterior contractor this is the single biggest gap
 *                   on the page — see OPEN ITEMS at the bottom of this file.
 *   TestimonialGrid `testimonials` is empty. ~800 five-star reviews exist and
 *                   not one verbatim quote was supplied, so none can ship.
 *   HoursTable      no published hours, so `showHours` is false and site.ts
 *                   emits no openingHoursSpecification either.
 *
 * There are NO FPO placeholders on this page. That is deliberate: an FPO field
 * in the hero of a contractor demo reads as an unfinished website, and the
 * drawn hero exists precisely so the page does not need one.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HeroElevation from "../components/sections/HeroElevation.astro";
import CredentialSchedule from "../components/sections/CredentialSchedule.astro";
import ServiceLegend from "../components/sections/ServiceLegend.astro";
import ProcessSteps from "../components/sections/ProcessSteps.astro";
import TitleBlock from "../components/sections/TitleBlock.astro";
import BeforeAfter from "../components/sections/BeforeAfter.astro";
import TestimonialGrid from "../components/sections/TestimonialGrid.astro";
import FAQ from "../components/sections/FAQ.astro";
import LocationContact from "../components/sections/LocationContact.astro";
import CTABand from "../components/sections/CTABand.astro";

import { SITE } from "../config/site";
import { localized } from "../lib/content";
import { useTranslations, localeFromUrl } from "../i18n/ui";

const locale = localeFromUrl(Astro.url);
const t = useTranslations(locale);

const services = await localized("services", locale);
const credentials = await localized("credentials", locale);
const process = await localized("process", locale);
const faqs = await localized("faq", locale);
const projects = await localized("projects", locale);
const reviews = await localized("testimonials", locale);

/**
 * Service-area list, VERBATIM from the intake. Not expanded, not tidied into
 * "Southern California", not given a radius we cannot support.
 */
const AREAS = [
  "Greater Los Angeles",
  "San Diego",
  "Orange County",
  "Riverside County",
  "Ventura County",
  "San Bernardino",
];

/**
 * Client-published scale claims. Rendered exactly as the client states them,
 * including the hedges — "3,000+" not "over 3,000", "around 800" not "800".
 *
 * OPEN ITEM: the operator flagged all three for re-verification before this is
 * sent. If any cannot be confirmed, DELETE THE ROW. Do not soften it.
 */
const FIGURES = [
  { value: "3,000+", label: "homeowners served" },
  { value: "~800", label: "five-star reviews" },
  { value: "10+", label: "years on exteriors" },
];

const TERMS = ["Free consultations", "Financing available"];

const callLabel = `${t("cta.call")} ${SITE.phone}`;
const callHref = `tel:${SITE.phoneHref}`;

const navLinks = [
  { label: "The work", href: "#services" },
  { label: "How it goes", href: "#process" },
  { label: "Questions", href: "#faq" },
  { label: "Contact", href: "#contact" },
];

/** FAQPage JSON-LD — only ever emitted for Q&As the page visibly renders. */
const faqSchema = faqs.map((f) => ({
  question: f.data.question,
  answer: f.data.answer,
}));
---

{/* SEOHead prefixes SITE.name on the homepage, so `title` must not repeat it. */}
<BaseLayout
  title="Siding, windows, stucco & roofing in the San Fernando Valley"
  description="Exterior only: James Hardie siding, Andersen and Pella windows, stucco, exterior paint, roofing and shutters. Canoga Park, CA. Free consultation — (877) 792-9082."
  path="/"
  navLinks={navLinks}
  faq={faqSchema}
>
  <HeroElevation
    id="top"
    eyebrow="Front elevation · exterior only"
    heading="You're the only one who never sees the outside of your house."
    body="Siding, windows, stucco, paint, roofing, shutters. Nothing on the inside. The consultation is free and somebody actually walks the house with you."
    ctaLabel={callLabel}
    ctaHref={callHref}
    note="Canoga Park · 6 counties"
    callouts={services.map((s) => s.data.short ?? s.data.name)}
    dimension="The part everyone else sees"
    drawingAlt="Line drawing of the front elevation of a house, with the six exterior trades called out on leader lines: siding on the gable, windows, stucco on the main wall, painting and texture coating on the garage door, roofing on the rake, and shutters beside the front window."
  />

  <CredentialSchedule
    items={credentials}
    label="Certified, listed and licensed"
    tone="sunken"
  />

  <ServiceLegend
    id="services"
    eyebrow="Legend"
    heading="Six things, all of them outdoors."
    body="Every item on the drawing above, in order. There is no seventh — no kitchens, no bathrooms, no additions."
    items={services}
    note="Not a general remodeler. Exterior envelope only."
  />

  {
    /* Renders the moment `src/content/projects/` has a before/after pair.
       See OPEN ITEMS — this is the highest-value missing section on the page. */
    projects.length > 0 && (
      <BeforeAfter
        eyebrow="Same house"
        heading="Before, and from the street."
        items={projects}
        tone="sunken"
      />
    )
  }

  <ProcessSteps
    id="process"
    eyebrow="What happens when you call"
    heading="Four steps, and you can stop after any of them."
    steps={process}
    layout="row"
    tone="sunken"
    ctaLabel={callLabel}
    ctaHref={callHref}
  />

  <TitleBlock
    id="record"
    label="Company record"
    areasLabel="Areas served"
    areas={AREAS}
    figuresLabel="On record"
    figures={FIGURES}
    termsLabel="Terms"
    terms={TERMS}
    tone="dark"
  />

  {
    /* Renders the moment `src/content/testimonials/` has verbatim reviews.
       Never invent one to fill this (CLAUDE.md §11). */
    reviews.length > 0 && (
      <TestimonialGrid
        locale={locale}
        eyebrow="From the neighbours"
        heading="What people said afterwards."
        items={reviews}
        columns={3}
      />
    )
  }

  <FAQ
    id="faq"
    locale={locale}
    eyebrow="Before you call"
    heading="The questions people actually ask."
    items={faqs}
  />

  <LocationContact
    id="contact"
    locale={locale}
    eyebrow="Canoga Park"
    heading="Where the shop is."
    body="The trucks go out from Eton Avenue. Call and someone will come out and walk the outside of the house with you."
    showHours={false}
    tone="sunken"
    formSubject="Exterior consultation request"
  />

  <CTABand
    heading="Have someone look at the outside of your house."
    body="Free consultation. Tell us what is bothering you about it and we will tell you what is actually failing."
    ctaLabel={callLabel}
    ctaHref={callHref}
    note="Financing available · CA Lic. #952272"
    align="split"
    tone="brand"
  />
</BaseLayout>

{
  /*
  ============================================================================
  OPEN ITEMS — CLOSE THESE BEFORE SENDING
  ============================================================================

  BLOCKING — the page is honest without them, but weaker:

  1. PHOTOGRAPHS. Zero supplied. `input/photos/` is empty. For an exterior
     contractor the before/after pair is the product, and its absence is the
     single biggest gap on this page. To fix: drop matched pairs into
     src/assets/images/ as job-before.jpg / job-after.jpg, add one JSON entry
     per job to src/content/projects/ with title, beforePhoto, beforeAlt,
     photo, alt, location, year. BeforeAfter then renders itself, in place,
     between the legend and the process. Six pairs is plenty.

  2. REVIEWS. Zero verbatim quotes supplied. The intake says ~800 five-star
     reviews exist and names two reviewers (Kimberly A., Sue H.) with no text.
     Six to ten real ones, with first name + last initial, rating and month,
     into src/content/testimonials/ and the section appears. Never write one.

  3. A NAMED FACE. Nobody is named anywhere — not on their site, not in the
     intake. In this trade an owner's name and photograph is the highest-trust
     element available and there is currently no substitute for it on the page.
     `people` collection + ProviderBios if the operator can get it.

  MUST VERIFY — each is currently on the page as the client publishes it:

  4. CSLB LICENCE #952272 — confirm on the Contractors State License Board
     public licence check. It appears in the footer, the trust bar, the FAQ,
     the title block stamp and the closing band. If it is wrong it is wrong in
     five places.

  5. THE THREE FIGURES in FIGURES above — 3,000+ homeowners, ~800 five-star
     reviews, 10+ years. If any cannot be confirmed, delete that row from the
     array rather than softening the wording.

  6. THE SIX CREDENTIALS in src/content/credentials/ — James Hardie Elite,
     Andersen Certified, Pella partner, Qualified Remodeler Top 500 (2025),
     Home Improvement Pro 200 (2025), BBB A+. All client-published, none
     embellished. Confirm the two 2025 awards are current.

  MISSING FACTS — sections are switched off rather than guessed:

  7. HOURS. Not published anywhere. site.ts HOURS is empty, LocationContact
     has showHours={false}, and no openingHoursSpecification is emitted.

  8. GEO COORDINATES. site.ts `geo` is null so the LocalBusiness schema omits
     it rather than pin the wrong unit on Eton Avenue. Paste them from the
     Google Business Profile.

  9. EMAIL. Not published. SITE.email is empty so the contact block omits it.

 10. SOCIAL / DIRECTORY URLS. The intake says Angi, HomeAdvisor, Houzz and
     Yelp but supplied no URLs. All four are empty, so nothing wrong lands in
     `sameAs`.

 11. FORM_ENDPOINT. Empty, so ContactForm renders its disabled state. Point it
     at a Formspree or Web3Forms endpoint before the client is asked to test.

  CONSIDERED AND DECLINED:

 12. SPANISH. The Valley has a large Spanish-speaking homeowner base and
     bilingual would be a real differentiator here. Declined for this pass
     because every word of a licensed trade's advertising has to be the
     operator's own, not a machine translation. One content pass if wanted.

 13. BONDING AND INSURANCE. Not claimed anywhere on this page, in any wording,
     because the client claims neither. Do not add it (CLAUDE.md §11).
  ============================================================================
  */
}
